# Atlas SEO (GetPronounce / Global / Sound)

## Do

- **One niche per domain** — getpronounce = Chinese *pronunciation* for English speakers. Global = vocab *charts* by target language. Sound = English *pronunciation*.
- **Tool pages** — each URL is a listenable chart (words + audio + pin image). That is the product.
- **Concrete copy** — cite the words on *this* page, pinyin, accent slots (“CN / TW / HK voices”). Use catalog data, not generic listicles.
- **Differentiation** — our multi-accent TTS matrix and pin-linked word sets are the moat; mention them where natural.

## Do not

- Mass-generate thin SEO pages with no audio or duplicate templates (“10 ways to learn Chinese”).
- Blur niches (random blog posts, unrelated languages on getpronounce.net).
- Compete on generic advice posts everyone else publishes — Google rewards original utility (working audio tools) and real on-page data.

## Pinterest

SEO page live **before** pin. Destination = site URL only (never homepage fallback). See `pinterest-vocab-seo-links.mdc` pattern.
